Author: Hongjie Jiang [aut], Anchi Che [aut], Yanxiao Han [aut] (co-corresponding author), Yanshuo Han [aut, cre] (co-corresponding author)
Maintainer: Yanshuo Han <yanshuohan@dlut.edu.cn>
Description: Distributional regression for RNA-seq based on the
    three-parameter Generalized Gamma (GG) family. The core engine
    sgcbDReg() fits gene-wise GG GLMs with arbitrary design matrices:
    a mean channel log(beta) = X b via blockwise Fisher scoring, an
    optional dispersion channel log(alpha) = W d via likelihood-ratio
    testing for differential variability (DV), and empirical-Bayes
    moderated t-tests for differential expression (DE). The legacy
    two-group entry point sgcbDE() remains fully backward-compatible.
    Preprocessing uses TMM normalization; inference uses limma-style
    fitFDist variance shrinkage. C++17/OpenMP parallelized throughout.
